+This article describes the training configuration for NeRF-based models using the Nerfstudio library, specifically leveraging NerfAcc and Instant-NGP for fast convergence on static scenes [S2]. It also details the specific architectural and optimization setup of Control-NeRF, which replaces standard positional encoding of 3D positions with sampled feature vectors [S1]. The configuration builds on the core differentiable volume rendering pipeline defined in [NeRF Training Loop](1522-training-loop-setup.md), optimizing a coarse network followed by a fine network using importance sampling and feature-volume inputs [S1]. It differs from standard NeRF by using 64-dimensional feature vectors instead of raw coordinates for the fine network input [S1].
 
